    "node-196v4e3": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The claim that 'Maintenance acceptance signature was not yet signed at notification time' is asserted based on the detail stating M-A had not accepted the boundary. However, evidence source 7e69d300-c57e-40a8-bb37-35a61073ff33#1 explicitly states that 'boundary acceptance pending' for M-A and notes a maintenance work order being scheduled is not proof of release. The incident description confirms the team was preparing (not yet released). While this seems supported, the target's proposed status relies on interpreting 'preparing' as equivalent to 'pending signature'. Evidence does not explicitly show the timestamp of notification relative to the exact moment acceptance would have been required or if a specific procedural step failed at that precise instant. The evidence supports M-A was pending but lacks explicit proof linking this directly to the air loss event's causality without assuming procedure violation.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "Explicit record showing the time 'notification' occurred and whether it preceded, coincided with, or followed any required acceptance step for boundary release; confirmation of what specific action constituted 'acceptance'.",
      "question": "What is the exact timestamp of the air-low notification relative to when M-A was expected to sign off on maintenance acceptance? Does a work order being scheduled constitute an implicit acceptance in this context?"
    },
    "node-hddaa6": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The claim that 'Temporary instruction attachment field was blank at issue time' is asserted based on the detail stating no approved temp instruction existed. Evidence source 7e69d300-c57e-40a8-bb37-35a61073ff33#1 states a daily briefing topic line exists but contains 'no valve-by-valve content'. It does not explicitly confirm the physical attachment field was blank or that an instruction *should* have been attached for this specific boundary change. The evidence supports lack of detailed content, not necessarily absence of required temporary instructions.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "Visual inspection record or system log confirming whether a temporary instruction document existed in the work package cover's attachment field at issue time; definition of what constitutes an 'approved temp instruction' for this specific boundary change type.",
      "question": "Was there any physical or digital placeholder, draft, or approved temporary instruction attached to WO-527? What criteria define a required temporary instruction for a routing update in ECP-1SC-04 rev 3?"
    },
